  "result": "Perfect! All 110 tests pass. I've successfully implemented VAT calculation for the invoicing system:\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`src/invoices.js`** - Updated `invoiceTotals()`:\n   - Now returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`\n   - Calculates VAT per line on amount after discount\n   - Uses `roundCents()` for each line's VAT\n   - total = subtotal - discount + vat\n   - All amounts clamped at 0\n\n2. **`src/render.js`** - Updated `renderInvoiceText()`:\n   - Shows VAT line (\u20acX.XX) when vat > 0\n   - Positioned just above the total line\n   - Uses `formatEuros()` for VAT display\n\n**VAT Calculation Logic:**\n- For each line: VAT = roundCents(net_amount \u00d7 vatRate / 100)\n- net_amount = gross_amount - line_discount  \n- Invoice VAT = sum of all rounded line VATs (not a percentage of invoice total)\n- Final total = subtotal - discount + vat\n\n**Test Coverage (110 total):**\n- 8 comprehensive VAT calculation tests\n- 11 render tests (updated for VAT display)\n- All existing tests updated to account for VAT in totals\n- Tests verify correct VAT rounding, different rates (0%, 9%, 21%), and discount + VAT interactions\n\nKey design decision: VAT is calculated **per line** after **per-line discounts**, ensuring proper rounding and transparency in how taxes are applied.",
